<section class="bhd-page__steps" aria-label="How to prepare Best Hydrate">
  <article class="bhd-page__step"><h2>1. Start with clean water</h2><p>Use potable water and a clean bottle, shaker or glass. In travel, field or humanitarian settings, safe water comes before drink formulation.</p></article>
  <article class="bhd-page__step"><h2>2. Measure one scoop</h2><p>Use 1 scoop for one prepared serving. If a newer physical label differs, follow the package in hand.</p></article>
  <article class="bhd-page__step"><h2>3. Add 500 mL of water</h2><p>Prepare one scoop in 500 mL of water. Do not concentrate the powder to chase stronger flavour or a larger electrolyte dose.</p></article>
  <article class="bhd-page__step"><h2>4. Mix until dispersed</h2><p>Close and shake a bottle, or stir thoroughly in a glass, until the powder is evenly mixed. Re-mix if material settles during storage or use.</p></article>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__split">
  <div class="bhd-page__split-media">
    <img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/3764014/pexels-photo-3764014.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1500" alt="Person carrying a reusable water bottle outdoors" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
